    {
        "content": "<p>Upload that json file to the web app to explore this visualisation interactively, and find out which directories are not covered in the overview at all.</p>",
        "id": 585853585,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776332657
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Kudos to <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1004599\">@Andrew Peterson</span> for making this super easy to visualize! <span aria-label=\"octopus\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f419\" role=\"img\" title=\"octopus\">:octopus:</span></p>",
        "id": 585853996,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776332793
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Set theory feels niche enough to not get much attention in the overview. That said, if I had to choose what to highlight, I'd add <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Cardinal.aleph#doc\">docs#Cardinal.aleph</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Order.cof#doc\">docs#Order.cof</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.CNF#doc\">docs#Ordinal.CNF</a>, and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.IsFundamentalSeq#doc\">docs#Ordinal.IsFundamentalSeq</a>. If we ever get club/stationary sets, I'd add those too.</p>",
        "id": 586254810,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776495791
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(So essentially, I'm asking if a PR adding those items would be welcome)</p>",
        "id": 586255086,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776496059
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"459227\">Violeta Hernández</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Missing.20items.20in.20the.20library.20overview/near/586255086\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(So essentially, I'm asking if a PR adding those items would be welcome)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think the answer is almost always yes!</p>",
        "id": 586257839,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1776499306
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38199\">#38199</a></p>",
        "id": 586259517,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776501134
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I believe <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=DedekindCut#doc\">docs#DedekindCut</a> should also be in the overview, but I have no idea where to put it.</p>",
        "id": 586260289,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776502071
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>More items which could be added: Newton's method (Dynamics/Newton); Prüfer subgroup (Dynamics/Prufer), topological entropy, ergodic group actions.<br>\n<span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"320882\">@Damien Thomine</span> I see you contributed quite a bit there. A PR adding these items (and any others I will have missed) to the overview is very welcome!</p>",
        "id": 586260805,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1776502694
    }
]